          ]
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "crypto/x509's chain verification with untrusted intermediates runs when a Go program verifies a peer's certificate as a TLS client. Caddy in this image never does: deploy/Caddyfile sets auto_https off (no ACME), serves its own certificate from /data/certs, and proxies to plain-http upstreams on localhost (reverse_proxy to the Flask backend and the central server); it verifies no certificate. Fixed upstream in Go 1.26.10 / 1.27.3; the Caddy build moved to golang:1.27.3-alpine on 2026-11-05 (the release after 4.0.1, docs/security/urgent-updates.md), so the flawed stdlib is no longer in the image and this statement covers the releases built with 1.27.2.",
      "status_notes": "Decided by maintainer."
    },
