      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_present",
      "impact_statement": "The vulnerable code is the sqlite3 command-line shell's .recover command (shell.c), and the shell is not in the image: only sqlite-libs (libsqlite3.so.0) is installed, the `sqlite` RPM that ships /usr/bin/sqlite3 is not, and `command -v sqlite3` finds nothing - deploy/Containerfile's runtime stage checks both at build time. The backend uses the library alone (Python's sqlite3 module for its databases), which has no .recover and runs no dot-commands. Node's bundled SQLite (node:sqlite, the nodejs.org binary) is library code too, with no .recover in its API. Nothing in the image can run the shell's recovery output.",
      "status_notes": "Decided by maintainer."
